    <p class="prose__lead">William Ashmore is a Florida native who has been fishing Tampa Bay and Central Florida for more than 40 years. Gatorbacks Fishing Charters is his own outfit, so the captain who answers your call is the one who runs your trip.</p>

    <h2>Tell Him What You Want to Catch</h2>
    <p>Four decades on these waters means there's usually a plan for whatever you have in mind. In the bay that can be redfish along the mangroves or snook around the shorelines. Past the beaches it's grouper, snapper and hogfish, and in the summer it's tarpon around the bridges and passes. When the lakes around Kissimmee are on, he runs crappie trips there too.</p>

    <h2>Licensed, and Everything's on the Boat</h2>
    <p>Capt. Ashmore holds a USCG 100 ton Master license. Your fishing license, rods, reels, bait and tackle are covered, and he cleans your fish at the end of the day so they go home ready to cook. You bring drinks (no glass), snacks, sunglasses and sunscreen.</p>
    <p>Guests have described him as having "lots of knowledge with a calm cool demeanor," which is what you want whether it's your first fish or your hundredth.</p>

    <p>Questions before you book? Call or text <a class="strong blue" href="{{ site.phoneHref }}">{{ site.phone }}</a>. If he's out fishing, he'll get back to you once he's off the water.</p>
